{{also|Testudo}}
==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|la|testūdō||tortoise, turtle, lyre, type of military shelter}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|testudoes|testudines}}

# {{lb|en|historical|Roman antiquity}} A [[shelter]] formed by a body of [[troop]]s by holding their [[shield]]s or [[target]]s close together over their heads.
# A shelter of similar shape for [[miner]]s, etc.
# {{lb|en|music}} A kind of [[lyre]]; so called in allusion to the lyre of Mercury, fabled to have been made of the shell of a tortoise.
# An [[encysted]] [[tumour]].
# {{lb|en|anatomy}} The [[fornix]].

